.TH "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_revoke_host_access" 9 "nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_revoke_host_access" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_revoke_host_access \- Initialize passthru command for Manage Exported NVM Subsystem Send - Revoke Host Access (message-based transports only)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" nvme_init_manage_export_nvms_send_revoke_host_access
.BI "(struct libnvme_passthru_cmd *cmd "  ","
.BI "struct nvme_exported_subsys_mgmt_data *data "  ","
.BI "__u32 len "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "cmd" 12
Passthru command to use
.IP "data" 12
Subsystem Management data buffer, see \fIstruct
nvme_exported_subsys_mgmt_data\fP
.IP "len" 12
Length of \fIdata\fP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Initializes the passthru command buffer for the Manage Exported NVM
Subsystem Send command with SEL value
NVME_MANAGE_EXPORT_NVMS_SEND_SEL_REVOKE_HOST_ACCESS. Command Dword 14
(ESUBIDV/ESUBID) is not used by this operation - the target Exported NVM
Subsystem(s) are specified in \fIdata\fP.
